The `conditional` rule assumes `params.rules` is iterable; if it’s missing or not an array, `for (const conditionalRule of rules)` will throw at runtime. Validate `rules` is an array before iterating, and consider running conditional rules through `validateRule` (not `validateBuiltInRule`) so custom/async validators work inside conditional rules too.
